/Type /Annot
/V (Beatriz Echauz \174 CP\13712\055CP\13723 \174 19 October 2026\012\012OBJECTIVE\012I aim to maximise eight unknown functions with a limited evaluation budget\072 one new input per function per round\056 Inputs have two to eight coordinates\056 I observe the returned numerical result but cannot inspect the underlying function\056\012\012CURRENT EVIDENCE\012My dataset contains 175 supplied observations plus 88 evaluations from eleven completed rounds\072 263 evaluated input\055output pairs\056 Function\055specific datasets contain 21 to 51 observations\056 Eight round\05512 queries are prepared and validated\073 their outcomes are not yet available\056\012\012HOW MY PROCESS FITS TOGETHER\012I validate the cumulative data\054 compare the latest outputs with the previous best\054 and review historical prediction errors\056 I then fit a separate Gaussian Process \050GP\051 to each function using a Matern kernel and target normalisation\056\012\012The GP estimates a predicted result and uncertainty\056 I rank candidate inputs using UCB \075 predicted mean \053 2 x predictive standard deviation\056 This balances promising predictions with opportunities to learn in uncertain regions\056\012\012Currently\054 I compare 100\054000 global candidates with 10\054000 candidates in each of two local boxes around the best observation\056 I validate the selected coordinates\054 retain their predictions\054 and prepare six\055decimal strings for manual portal submission\056\012\012Only returned evaluations count as results\056 A high UCB is a reason to test a point\054 not a guarantee of improvement\056)
>>
endobj
