/T (Identify which principles or heuristics now guide your query decisions)
/TU (Identify which principles or heuristics now guide your query decisions)
/Type /Annot
/V (FROM A BASELINE TO A DOCUMENTED WORKFLOW\012In CP\13712\054 I used GP\055UCB with global random candidate search\056 Subsequent notebooks compared original and wider kernel bounds\054 responding to fitted parameters reaching their limits\056 A boundary warning motivated investigation rather than proving a model was wrong\056\012\012CP\13714 added linear and RBF SVM diagnostics\056 CP\13715\055CP\13717 compared classification and regression approaches\054 including linear models and small neural networks\056 These experiments helped distinguish predictive checks from the continuous optimisation objective\056 The current auxiliary models are an eight\055unit neural network for F5 and linear regression for F7\073 they do not supply UCB uncertainty\056\012\012CP\13718 compared Matern smoothness and bound configurations using cross\055validation RMSE\056 Later notebooks retained the selected configurations while re\055estimating continuous kernel parameters as feedback arrived\056 Global and local proposals made the exploration\055versus\055refinement choice explicit\056\012\012CP\13719 compared simple and structured prompts around supplied candidate data\056 Numerical candidate ranking remained in Python\056 CP\13721 strengthened transparency and documentation\073 CP\13722 added regional distance diagnostics and an F5 minimum\055distance constraint\056 CP\13723 added PCA and reproducible candidate seeds that vary by function and round\056\012\012WHAT NOW GUIDES MY DECISIONS\012I use observed progress\054 prediction errors\054 candidate distances and model disagreement\056 I preserve negative and near\055zero outputs\054 avoid double\055counting cumulative feedback\054 and separate completed experiments from planned changes\056 No function improved in round 11\054 reinforcing the need to examine redundancy and uncertainty rather than equating more data with automatic gains\056)
>>
endobj
