/V (OBSERVED PROGRESS THROUGH ROUND 11\012Seven functions improved over their initial best\056 Values below are rounded and must be compared within each function\072\012\012Function     Initial best          Current best\012F1               7\05671e\05516              7\05671e\05516\012F2               0\056611205              0\056658240\012F3              \0550\056034835             \0550\056030964\012F4              \0554\056025542              0\056615273\012F5               1088\05686                8515\05638\012F6              \0550\056714265             \0550\056242431\012F7               1\056364968              2\056436323\012F8               9\056598482              9\056958227\012\012Progress is uneven\072 five functions improved in round 1\054 two in round 10\054 and none in round 11\056 These counts do not measure the size of gains or establish convergence\056\012\012PATTERNS AND THEIR LIMITS\012F5\047s strongest observations are near the upper input boundaries\056 F4 has a repeatedly sampled promising interior region\073 F6\047s best point has its fifth coordinate close to zero\056 These associations reflect adaptive sampling and do not establish causal variable importance\056\012\012PCA describes input variation\054 not output sensitivity\056 The first two components retain 55\0561\045 of input variance for F7 and 47\0560\045 for F8\056 Five and seven components are needed for 90\045\054 respectively\054 so I retained all coordinates\056\012\012For F3\054 x3 has a small PC1 weight but a short GP length scale\056 This contrast shows why a low\055variance input direction can still matter to the objective\056 F1\047s extremely small outputs also mean rank colours can exaggerate practically tiny differences\056)
>>
endobj
