/V (BALANCING EXPLORATION AND EXPLOITATION\012UCB rewards both predicted performance and uncertainty\056 For round 12\054 the highest eligible scores select global proposals for F1\054 F3 and F7\054 and local proposals for F2\054 F4\054 F5\054 F6 and F8\056 Search labels describe candidate generation\054 not proven global or local optima\056\012\012EXAMPLE 1\072 REDUCING REPETITION IN F5\012A round\05510 query only about 0\056000235 from an earlier observation improved the best output by 5\056089\054 to 8515\056379\056 The gain was real but small\056 In round 11\054 I required a Euclidean separation of at least 0\05601\073 the selected point returned 8311\056706 and did not improve the best\056\012\012The constraint therefore has no demonstrated performance advantage\056 The unsubmitted alternative was not evaluated\054 so its result is unknown\056 I retained the constraint for round 12 to reduce repetition\072 separation is 0\056010475\054 at a UCB reduction of 0\056715\045 versus the unconstrained winner\056\012\012EXAMPLE 2\072 ACCURACY IS NOT IMPROVEMENT\012For F7 in round 11\054 the GP predicted 2\056388085 and observed 2\056351393\072 absolute error about 0\0560367\056 Linear regression predicted 1\056206557\054 an error about 1\0561448\056 The GP was more accurate at this point\054 but the output still fell below the incumbent 2\056436323\056\012\012HANDLING SURPRISES\012I retain unsuccessful evaluations\054 refit the models and record bound warnings\056 Error divided by predicted standard deviation is a diagnostic\054 not a full calibration test\056 White\055noise contributions and model mismatch mean predictive uncertainty is not entirely reducible through more sampling\056)
>>
endobj
