/V (NEXT\072 THE FINAL ROUND IN MODULE 24\012When round\05512 feedback arrives\054 I will match it to the submitted coordinates\054 compare predictions with observations and update the best\055so\055far history\056 I will examine whether distant proposals discovered useful regions and whether nearby proposals added meaningful gains\056\012\012For the final submission\054 I will consider local refinement around newly successful points\054 while preserving exploration where predictions remain weak\056 I will reassess F5\047s distance constraint using the accumulated evidence rather than assuming that greater separation is always beneficial\056\012\012PLANNED EXPERIMENTS\012Subject to the remaining budget\054 I would compare UCB with Expected Improvement on identical candidate pools and examine sensitivity to the exploration weight and kernel bounds\056 These are proposed comparisons\054 not completed results\056 I would record the configurations and costs and avoid treating an untested candidate\047s acquisition score as validation\056\012\012CONNECTION TO BROADER MACHINE LEARNING\012This workflow resembles sequential experimental design in settings where evaluations are expensive\054 such as process tuning or laboratory optimisation\056 Its practical value depends on reproducible decisions\054 useful uncertainty estimates and careful separation of prediction from evidence\056 PCA and model comparisons support interpretation\054 but neither removes sampling bias nor proves that benchmark results transfer to a real industry\056\012\012COMMUNICATING TO A NON\055TECHNICAL STAKEHOLDER\012I would say\072 \042We improved the best result in seven of eight tasks\054 but progress has slowed and the latest completed round produced no new best results\056 We choose each next test using both expected performance and what remains uncertain\073 the next eight outcomes are still unknown\056\042\012\012Evidence\072 CP\13712\055CP\13723 notebooks and recorded outputs\056\012Project\072 github\056com\057BeatrizEchauz\057bbo\055capstone\012The public repository may lag this local CP\13723 snapshot\056)
>>
endobj
